                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope's Notes: James Pearsall silk manufacturer of London and Taunton
                            Sun Fire 1802 54 Bread St, 1814 3 Charles St City Rd 1815 145 Cheapside
                            will PCC 1841 James Pearsall silkman 145 Cheapside, will PCC 1846 James
                            Pearsall late silkman now gent of Clerkenwell, will PCC 1848 Rebecca
                            Pearsall widow of Islington. A James Pearsall Esq was a steward 1812 for
                            Lancaster's system of education, a common councilman Faringdon Within
                            1816, member of Socy for Encoragement Arts, Manufctrs, Commerce 1817.
                            There was also a James Pearsall attorney of 21 Holborn Court Grays Inn
                            1800 Law List</p>
